  "details": "I don't really understand the choice of having the master volume be able to be cranked up to 125% instead of just allowing the user to use 125% for any of the audio sub-categories.\n\nI raise this because the only time I've ever used the 125% volume feature, it's been to crank-up the world volume because a movie is too quiet. However, doing so means I now have to lower voice, avatar, and UI volumes so that they're not deafening.\n\nI suggest flipping this, allowing the user to set 125% for independent channels and 100% be the maximum for Master.\n\nEither that or -- Why is there a \"125%\" to begin with? Just make the 125 the new 100 across the board and adjust the volume defaults accordingly. In my mind this is the way it ought to be, 100% should always be 100%. The only reason I'd provide more percentage steps is if I want to give the user more granular control over volume, but in that case I'd probably opt to use 0.5% steps rather than pretend there's a \"200%\" option.\n\nI don't hear any distortion or anything at 125%, so I assume you're not doing anything weird with the audio at that setting, as opposed to something like VLC where it does.\n\nIt's not a big deal or anything, just a bit of an annoyance and it seems like the kinda thing that maybe wouldn't take a lot of work to implement, so figured I'd pitch the idea.\n\nThanks!",
